{
  "_comment": [
    "BARE static-analyzer seccomp profile.",
    "Allowlist, not denylist: anything not named here returns EPERM. That is",
    "deliberate — a denylist silently admits every syscall added by a future",
    "kernel, and this file is the last line under cap_drop=ALL, read-only",
    "rootfs, uid 10001, and network_mode=none.",
    "",
    "Notably absent, and why: ptrace/process_vm_* (debugger primitives; the",
    "dynamic analyzer gets its own profile in M5), mount/umount2/pivot_root/",
    "chroot/unshare/setns and the fsopen/move_mount family (namespace and mount",
    "escapes), bpf/perf_event_open/kexec_load/init_module (kernel-level attack",
    "surface), add_key/keyctl/request_key (kernel keyring), userfaultfd (a",
    "classic exploitation primitive), io_uring_* (large, historically fragile",
    "attack surface, and no analyzer needs it), reboot/swapon/settimeofday/",
    "clock_settime/acct/quotactl (host-affecting).",
    "",
    "Socket syscalls ARE allowed. With network_mode=none there is no reachable",
    "network, AF_UNIX is needed by libc name resolution and the JVM, and",
    "returning EPERM there breaks tooling for no security gain.",
    "",
    "clone3 is explicitly ENOSYS rather than EPERM so glibc falls back to",
    "clone(); EPERM makes modern glibc abort instead."
  ],
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
  "archMap": [
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
      "subArchitectures": ["SCMP_ARCH_X86", "SCMP_ARCH_X32"]
    },
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_AARCH64",
      "subArchitectures": ["SCMP_ARCH_ARM"]
    }
  ],
